Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:30:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] input: add inertial scroll coasting for touchpads

When the finger lifts off the touchpad, scrolling stops dead because
no more axis events arrive. Track per-axis signed velocity (delta/ms)
and, after a short 24ms watchdog of silence, synthesize decaying axis
events for scroll_decel ms with a quadratic ease-out curve, macOS-style.

- per-axis state (vertical/horizontal) with EMA velocity
- coast seed velocity clamped, min-velocity gate to avoid drift on
  slow lifts
- any real motion on an axis cancels its coast immediately
- coast emits a clean zero-delta stop event when finished
- scroll_decel (Int, 0-1000, default 300ms) now wired; velocity units
  fixed to delta/ms so scroll_accel_speed behaves as documented
